reac-labtools is the numpy/scipy signal-analysis bench for captured Roland
REAC (audio-over-Ethernet, EtherType 0x8819) traffic: heterodyne pitch and
clock-wobble meters, spectrum classification, per-channel decode health,
glitch and A/B defect detection, plus the rig scripts that produce the
captures those meters read.

It is the dependency-carrying counterpart to reac-tools, which stays pure
standard library. See README.md for the split.

## Third-party code and references

All source files in this repository are original works. No third-party
code is copied or otherwise included; this repository therefore carries
no third-party copyright. numpy and scipy are runtime dependencies used
through their public APIs; no numpy or scipy source is vendored here.

### Protocol facts referenced (no code reused, no upstream copyright)

The REAC wire framing these tools decode was reverse-engineered and
documented by the projects below. reac-labtools re-implements those
documented facts in original Python -- locating the 0x8819 EtherType,
stripping any 802.1Q tag, reading the 16-bit little-endian sequence
counter from the first two payload bytes, and unpacking the 24-bit
sample-major PCM slots -- without copying any code or structure from them:

- per-gron/reacdriver -- GPL-3.0. The original REAC reverse-engineering
  (macOS driver). Documents the wire framing: EtherType 0x8819, the 16-bit
  little-endian sequence counter at payload bytes 0-1, the 0xC2 0xEA end
  marker, and the 1492-byte frame.
- norihiro/obs-h8819-source -- GPL-3.0-or-later -- Copyright (C) 2022
  Norihiro Kamae <norihiro@nagater.net>. OBS REAC source plugin, framing
  taken from reacdriver. Confirms the same 16-bit little-endian
  l2_counter and per-frame +1 sequencing.
- norihiro/reaccapture -- GPL-3.0. Linux REAC pcap-to-WAV decoder; the
  s24be/s24le justification for the sample unpacking used here.

These facts inform the original implementations in reac_codec.py,
reac_frame_anatomy.py, decode_probe.py and the meters built on them.
None of these files derive from upstream code; they re-express publicly
documented protocol facts.

### Standards and specifications (facts, not copyrightable, no claim)

- libpcap classic savefile format -- file magic 0xA1B2C3D4, global and
  per-packet headers, read by original struct-based code; no libpcap
  code is used.
- IEEE 802.1Q -- VLAN tag layout, for stripping the phantom tag seen on
  bridge egress.

The interface facts of the Roland REAC protocol (EtherType, framing,
sequence counter) are stated as facts and carry no copyright claim by this
project.
